WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.500
An image is a grid of numbers. Here, zero means black, and two
hundred and fifty five means white.

2
00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:11.533
Keep the rows and columns in order. This image has two rows
and two columns.

3
00:00:11.533 --> 00:00:17.200
Multiply each pixel by one half. Every number halves, so the
image becomes darker.

4
00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:22.300
Now add ten to every pixel. This brightens the output without
changing its shape.

5
00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:28.933
Predict the new mean. Add the four output values and divide by
four. Pause here to work it out.

6
00:00:28.933 --> 00:00:33.567
The values sum to two hundred. Divide by four: the new mean is
fifty.

7
00:00:33.567 --> 00:00:40.533
The original mean was eighty. Halving it and adding ten gives
fifty. This same rule acts on every pixel.

